// wdoc section: Block Visibility.
page wdoc_visibility { sites = [:reference]  title = "Block Visibility"
  h1 "Block Visibility"

  p "Any block can carry an `@only(...)` or `@except(...)` decorator to scope it to a subset of the build — by site name, template kind, or output backend. Use `@only` to render a block *only* where the conditions match, and `@except` to render it *everywhere except* where they match."

  h2 "Axes"

  p "Both decorators take the same three optional arguments, each a list of symbols:"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Argument"   | "Matches against" |
      | "`sites`"     | "The site name — the label on a `site` block (`site marketing { … }` ⇒ `:marketing`)" |
      | "`templates`" | "The site's template kind: `:webpage`, `:book`, or `:presentation`" |
      | "`backends`"  | "The output target: `:html`, `:pdf`, `:markdown`, or `:skill`" |
  }

  callout "The skill target names itself" {
    class = ["info"]
    body  = "`wcl wdoc skill` runs the Markdown emitter but reports itself as `:skill`, so a skill folder and a Markdown site can be scoped apart. `@except(backends=[:markdown])` no longer hides a block from the skill build — say `[:markdown, :skill]` to hide it from both."
  }

  h2 "Examples"

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
page home {
  // Only on the `:marketing` site.
  @only(sites=[:marketing]) callout "Promo" { body = "Sign up today!" }

  // Everywhere except the printed PDF.
  @except(backends=[:pdf]) p "Watch the screencast above."

  // Only in slide decks.
  @only(templates=[:presentation]) p "Press → to continue."

  // Only on the web (HTML or Markdown), never the PDF.
  @only(backends=[:html, :markdown]) video { src = "demo.mp4" }
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Semantics"

  p "**Within an axis** the values are OR'd — `sites=[:a, :b]` matches site `a` or `b`. **Across axes** they are AND'd — `@only(sites=[:docs], templates=[:book])` renders only when the site is `docs` *and* its template is `book`."

  p "A block renders when `@only` (if present) matches **and** `@except` (if present) does *not* fully match. An axis whose current value is unknown — the synthetic unnamed site, or a site with no `default_template` — never matches, so an `@only` on that axis hides the block."

  callout "Template kind is per-site" {
    class = ["info"]
    body  = "Filtering on `templates` uses the site's `default_template`. A page-level `template` override does not change which template axis a block matches."
  }

  h2 "Waiving a block a target can't render"

  p "The `backends` axis is also how you answer the build when it refuses a block. A few blocks are implemented for some targets and not others — `markdown_source` previews a page's generated Markdown from inside the HTML build, and `file` ships a file into an output folder a single-file PDF doesn't have. Using one on a target it doesn't cover is a **build error**, naming the kind, the target and the fix:"

  code text {
    source = <<'TEXT'
× `file` has no :pdf implementation (it is native on :html, :markdown, :skill);
  remove the block or waive it here with `@except(backends = [:pdf])`
TEXT
  }

  p "The two halves say different things and the build wants both to agree: the block's `@native(backends = …)` declaration is a **capability** — what wdoc can render — and `@except(backends = …)` on your instance is your **intent** — that you don't want it there. Waive it and the build proceeds, rendering nothing for that block on that target:"

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
page overview { start = true
  // Shipped with the skill and linked from the web build; the print PDF
  // has nowhere to put the file, and we're fine with that.
  @except(backends=[:pdf])
  file "src/setup.sh" { dir = "scripts"  as = "run setup" }
}
WCL
  }

  p "The alternative is to move the block behind an `@only` so it never reaches that target in the first place. What you cannot do is nothing: a block that a target can't render used to vanish from that output silently, and this is the mechanism that ended it."
}
